{"nodes": [{"id": "aigen_backend_docs_general_flow_procurement_flow", "label": "PR to RFQ to QCF to PO Flow", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "One end-to-end pipeline with four roles (Vendor, DIC, CS, CL); all branches converge on SAP Auto PO creation, with manual iSourcing as the fallback for high-value or problematic items.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/GENERAL_FLOW.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_general_flow_status_milestone", "label": "status_milestone Field", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "A single numeric code carried by both rfqLibrary and qcfLibrary tracks workflow progression across 20+ states, so one column drives dashboards, filters and cron selection.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/GENERAL_FLOW.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_general_flow_status_vendor", "label": "status_vendor Field", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/GENERAL_FLOW.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_general_flow_status_dic", "label": "status_dic Field", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/GENERAL_FLOW.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_general_flow_tipe_rfq", "label": "tipe_rfq Classification", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Distinguishes the standard Auto PO path from isourcing, surrogate and revisi_oe exception paths without adding separate tables.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/GENERAL_FLOW.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_general_flow_sync_auto_po", "label": "syncAutoPO SAP PO Creation", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Triggered by CL approval or by the sync cron; selects qcf_approved=1 with is_sync null or 0, posts a header/item payload whose document type, incoterms and tax code branch on server group, then writes back po_number, is_sync and the SLA lead time.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/GENERAL_FLOW.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_general_flow_multi_vendor_fallback", "label": "Multi-Vendor Fallback lvl1 to lvl2", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "A declining or silent primary vendor must not stall the PR: decline duplicates the RFQ to vendor_lvl2 immediately, day 3 activates lvl2 on silence, and both silent at day 9 routes to iSourcing.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/GENERAL_FLOW.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_general_flow_cs_decision_matrix", "label": "CS Decision Matrix", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Four exits from CS review (proceed to QCF, surrogate, revise OE, iSourcing) give a human a route out of every exception state rather than letting items dead-end.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/GENERAL_FLOW.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_general_flow_cron_reminder_timeline", "label": "Day 3 6 9 Cron Reminder Timeline", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/GENERAL_FLOW.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_general_flow_vendor_token_access", "label": "Vendor Token-Based RFQ Access", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "The emailed JWT is checked for signature, presence in rfqTokenEmail, is_active and date_expired, and is deactivated on submission so a link cannot be reused.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/GENERAL_FLOW.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_general_flow_isourcing_routing", "label": "iSourcing Manual Procurement Routing", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "High-value items and stalled RFQs leave the automated path into iSourcing board_card and item_card rows, auto-assigned to a CL by material group.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/GENERAL_FLOW.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_general_flow_config_validation_table", "label": "config_validation Thresholds", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "price_item_idr decides RFQ versus iSourcing routing; Max_price and Min_price bound price deviation; the two SLA day values drive every deadline in the flow.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/GENERAL_FLOW.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_general_flow_dic_confirmation_stage", "label": "DIC Confirmation Stage", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "The requesting department confirms the quotation before procurement acts; accept above the price threshold diverts to OE revision, decline routes to CS, and request-revision resets the vendor status and bumps vendor_batch.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/GENERAL_FLOW.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "aigen_backend_docs_general_flow_procurement_flow", "target": "aigen_backend_docs_general_flow_status_milestone", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/GENERAL_FLOW.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "aigen_backend_docs_general_flow_procurement_flow", "target": "aigen_backend_docs